From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] avutil/hwcontext_v4l2request: refuse a size the driver shrinks

A decoder whose limit is not a box, such as an area in macroblocks,
enumerates sizes past it and shrinks the OUTPUT format S_FMT is given.
The frames were then set up at the smaller size, and the stream decoded
to nothing.

Read the OUTPUT format back and refuse a width or height smaller than
the stream's, as an unsupported frame size is refused.
---
diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
index 8752ccf..1fc7907 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -618,6 +618,19 @@ static int v4l2request_probe_video_device(AVHWFramesContext *hwfc,
         goto fail;
     }
 
+    // A driver whose limit is not a box, such as an area, shrinks the size it cannot decode
+    if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_MULTIPLANAR(fctxi->output.format.type) ?
+        fctxi->output.format.fmt.pix_mp.width < hwfc->width ||
+        fctxi->output.format.fmt.pix_mp.height < hwfc->height :
+        fctxi->output.format.fmt.pix.width < hwfc->width ||
+        fctxi->output.format.fmt.pix.height < hwfc->height) {
+        ret = AVERROR(EINVAL);
+        av_log(hwfc, AV_LOG_VERBOSE,
+               "Device %s is missing support for frame size %dx%d of pixelformat %s\n",
+               path, hwfc->width, hwfc->height, av_fourcc2str(pixelformat));
+        goto fail;
+    }
+
     // The capabilities again, now of the codec format: holding a CAPTURE buffer may depend on it
     buffers = (struct v4l2_create_buffers) {
         .count = 0,
